---
description: Testing conventions for unit, integration, and e2e tests
globs: **/*.spec.ts,**/*.test.ts,**/*.test.tsx,**/e2e/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# Testing

- Unit tests (Jest/Vitest): services and pure helpers; mock repositories and external clients.
- Integration tests: real Postgres, MongoDB, Redis via Testcontainers. No mocks for our own DB code.
- E2E (Playwright): critical user journeys only (login, see matches, track application).
- Test names describe behavior: `it('rejects an expired session')`.
- Cover failure paths: timeouts, duplicates, retries, invalid input, unauthorized access.
- Never weaken or delete a test to make it pass; fix the code or flag the spec.
- External HTTP (job sources, LLM) is stubbed with recorded fixtures.
